    "docid": "52160",
    "score": 52.67886467008983,
    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Technogym's Heritage in the Olympic Games\ndate: 2018-06-01\n---\nExplore Technogym's journey as the Official Supplier to the Olympic Games \u2013 from Sydney 2000 to Paris 2024 \u2013 continuously elevating athletic performance through innovation and excellence.\n\nAs Official Supplier, Technogym has provided its most innovative equipment and technology to the athletes' training centers for the last nine editions of the Games. This historical involvement with professional athletes and a variety of sporting disciplines has proved fundamental to the brand's ability to design innovative technology and products, gathering valuable insights and feedback from the champions.\n\nFor decades, Technogym has helped athletes all over the planet seize the highest achievements by leveraging the most advanced technology and knowledge of physical exercise. Today, the brand stands with them at prestigious sporting events worldwide and on the most ambitious playgrounds. Technogym's commitment to the Olympic Games goes far beyond the supply of equipment and technology: its association with the Olympics has become a powerful communication platform through which to leverage sports and achieve Technogym's ultimate mission: to involve the global population in physical exercise.\n\nTechnogym's Olympic Stories\n\nSYDNEY 2000\n\nSydney 2000 marked Technogym's first edition of the Olympic Games as Fitness Equipment Official Supplier. Each training center for each of the different disciplines was equipped with the latest products, including Selection Line, which was launched at the Games. This comprehensive range of selected strength equipment has become an icon of sport training. Selection \u2013 after several new releases integrating new technologies and digital capabilities \u2013 remains one of the most popular lines of equipment in the world to this day.\n\nATHENS 2004\n\nThe Athens 2004 Olympic Games were significant thanks to a growing focus on technology. A year earlier Technogym had launched the Wellness TV \u2013 the first TV screen integrated into cardio equipment \u2013 providing engaging entertainment options to users for the first time. Athletes at the Olympic Village were able to make use of this technology to enhance their training experience.\n\nTURIN 2006\n\nTechnogym first experienced the Winter Olympic Games with Turin 2006. In Turin, Technogym equipped several training centers within the urban venues downtown, dedicated to stadium sports such as hockey, speed skating, figure skating and more; while in the mountain area Technogym equipped two different Olympic Villages, one for alpine skiing and the other one for cross country ski and related disciplines. Skating and skill-intensive discipline athletes showed a strong interest in Kinesis"
  }
