 first Olympic basketball tournament.\n\nAmerican dominance\n\nThanks in part to the effort of Phog Allen\u2014a Kansas Jayhawks collegiate coach\u2014the first Olympic basketball tournament was organized in the 1936 Berlin Olympics on outdoor tennis courts. Dr. Naismith presented the medals to the top three teams. According to the Olympic rules of that time, all of the competitors were amateurs. The tournament"
