at which point it would become the third largest country in the world. By 2050, six countries are expected to exceed 300 million: China, India, Indonesia, Nigeria, Pakistan, and the USA.\n\nGrowing population in Africa\n\nWith the highest rate of population growth, Africa is expected to account for more than half of the world's population growth between 2015 and 2050.\n\nDuring this period, the populations of"
