e further divided into various subcategories.\n\nForerunners\n\nAthletes with disabilities at the Olympic Games\n\nAthletes with disabilities did compete at the Olympic Games prior to the advent of the Paralympics. The first athlete to do so was German-American gymnast George Eyser in 1904, who had one artificial leg. Oliv\u00e9r Halassy, a Hungarian amputee water polo player, competed in three successive Olympic Games, beginning in 1928. Hungarian K\u00e1roly Tak"
