medals were not awarded at the inaugural Olympics in 1896 in Athens, Greece. The winners were instead given a silver medal and an olive branch, whilst runners-up received a laurel branch and a copper or bronze medal.\"After this followed the distribution of the second prizes. The King presented each winner a bronze medal and a laure"
